; The xact command keeps a per-unit `@` cost: the drafted posting prints
; with its cost, and the balancing posting is inferred in the cost's
; commodity ($-60.00), as it is when the printed draft is parsed back.

2024/01/01 Grocery Store
    Expenses:Food    10 AAPL @ $5.00
    Assets:Cash   $-50.00

test xact 2024/06/15 Grocery to Expenses:Food '@' '$6.00' '10 AAPL' from Assets:Cash
2024/06/15 Grocery Store
    Expenses:Food                            10 AAPL @ $6.00
    Assets:Cash
end test
